###  https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#DangerousOccurrences
:DangerousOccurrences rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#Concept> ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "18/12/2020" ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Lucy" ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HSE Incident Management Framework - Guidance 2020" ;
                      rdfs:comment "Dangerous occurrences may result from a sequence of events and circumstances involving a combination of unsafe acts, unsafe conditions, system failures, human factors and/or omissions. It most directly relates to the term ‘reportable circumstance’ as defined by the WHO (2009)" ;
                      rdfs:label "DangerousOccurrences" ;
                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#definition> "Dangerous occurrences may result from a sequence of events and circumstances involving a combination of unsafe acts, unsafe conditions, system failures, human factors and/or omissions. It most directly relates to the term ‘reportable circumstance’ as defined by the WHO (2009)" ;
                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#prefLabel> "DangerousOccurrences" .


