###  https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#Findings
:Findings rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#Concept> ;
          <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "18/12/2020" ;
          <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Lucy" ;
          <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HSE Incident Management Framework - Guidance 2020" ;
          rdfs:comment "1) Factors that, if corrected, would likely have prevented the incident or mitigated the harm;2) Factors that if corrected, would not have prevented the incident or mitigated the harm, but are important for patient/staff safety or safe patient care in general (incidental findings); and3) Mitigating factors – factors that did not allow the incident to have more serious consequences and represent solid safeguards that should be kept in place.(Ref: Canadian Incident Analysis Framework – Canadian Patient Safety Institute 2012)" ;
          rdfs:label "Findings" ;
          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#definition> "1) Factors that, if corrected, would likely have prevented the incident or mitigated the harm;2) Factors that if corrected, would not have prevented the incident or mitigated the harm, but are important for patient/staff safety or safe patient care in general (incidental findings); and3) Mitigating factors – factors that did not allow the incident to have more serious consequences and represent solid safeguards that should be kept in place.(Ref: Canadian Incident Analysis Framework – Canadian Patient Safety Institute 2012)" ;
          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#prefLabel> "Findings" .


