                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#prefLabel> "Risk Assessment" .


###  https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#RiskAvoidance
:RiskAvoidance rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#Concept> ;
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "07/09/2020" ;
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Rob" ;
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HSE Part 1/ISO 31000:2009" ;
               rdfs:comment "Informed decision not to be involved in, or to withdraw from, an activity in order not to be exposed to a particular risk. Risk avoidance may increase the significance of other risks or may lead to the loss of opportunities for gain." ;
               rdfs:label "Risk Avoidance" ;
               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#definition> "Informed decision not to be involved in, or to withdraw from, an activity in order not to be exposed to a particular risk. Risk avoidance may increase the significance of other risks or may lead to the loss of opportunities for gain." ;
               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#prefLabel> "Risk Avoidance" .


###  https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#RiskCategories
:RiskCategories rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#Concept> ;
                <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "07/09/2020" ;
                <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Rob" ;
                <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HSE Part 1/ISO 31000:2009" ;
                rdfs:comment "The categories used by the organisation to group similar opportunities or risks for the purposes of reporting and assigning responsibility." ;
                rdfs:label "Risk Categories" ;
                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#definition> "The categories used by the organisation to group similar opportunities or risks for the purposes of reporting and assigning responsibility." ;
                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#prefLabel> "Risk Categories" .


###  https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#RiskCriteria
:RiskCriteria rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#Concept> ;
              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "07/09/2020" ;
              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Rob" ;
              <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HSE Part 1/ISO 31000:2009" ;
              rdfs:comment "Terms of reference against which the significance of a risk is evaluated." ;
              rdfs:label "Risk Criteria" ;
              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#definition> "Terms of reference against which the significance of a risk is evaluated." ;
              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#prefLabel> "Risk Criteria" .


###  https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#RiskDe-Escalation
:RiskDe-Escalation rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#Concept> ;
                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "12/09/2020" ;
                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Rob" ;
                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HSE Part 3" ;
                   rdfs:comment "In instances where a risk was notified to and accepted onto the register of a more Senior Manager for oversight it may be that following the implementation of actions the rating of the risk may have reduced to an acceptable or tolerable level or where remaining actions lie within the control of the Manager at the level below. In such circumstances a decision may be taken to ‘close’ the risk on the register and to de-escalate it onto the register of the Manager on the level below. Such risks when added to the register below are given a risk status of ‘open’ on that register and are reviewed at the next Management Team meeting of that Manager." ;
                   rdfs:label "Risk De-Escalation" ;
                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#definition> "In instances where a risk was notified to and accepted onto the register of a more Senior Manager for oversight it may be that following the implementation of actions the rating of the risk may have reduced to an acceptable or tolerable level or where remaining actions lie within the control of the Manager at the level below. In such circumstances a decision may be taken to ‘close’ the risk on the register and to de-escalate it onto the register of the Manager on the level below. Such risks when added to the register below are given a risk status of ‘open’ on that register and are reviewed at the next Management Team meeting of that Manager." ;
                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#prefLabel> "Risk De-Escalation" .


###  https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#RiskEvaluation
:RiskEvaluation rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#Concept> ;
                <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "07/09/2020" ;
                <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Rob" ;
                <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HSE Part 1/ISO 31000:2009" ;
                rdfs:comment "Process of comparing the results of risk analysis with risk criteria to determine whether the risk and/or its magnitude is acceptable or tolerable." ;
                rdfs:label "Risk Evaluation" ;
                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#definition> "Process of comparing the results of risk analysis with risk criteria to determine whether the risk and/or its magnitude is acceptable or tolerable." ;
                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#prefLabel> "Risk Evaluation" .


###  https://ark.adaptcentre.ie/Ontologies/ARKHealthTerminology#RiskIdentification
:RiskIdentification rdf:type owl:NamedIndividual ,
                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#Concept> ;
                    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "07/09/2020" ;
                    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Rob" ;
                    <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "HSE Part 1/ISO 31000:2009" ;
                    rdfs:comment "A systematic process applied to the organisation’s objectives and activities to identify possible risk sources and causes and potential consequences or impacts should a risk occur." ;
                    rdfs:label "Risk Identification" ;
                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#definition> "A systematic process applied to the organisation’s objectives and activities to identify possible risk sources and causes and potential consequences or impacts should a risk occur." ;
                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos#prefLabel> "Risk Identification" .


